The two new helpers fork the accepted CTF02 whole-call transports. They retain
exact CTF01 literal unit39/42 inputs and fixed CON15/195 loader inputs. Production
whole Construct call counts remain dynamic actual observations. Original public
loader phases, source stop outcomes, diagnostics and owner snapshots stay intact.
The CTF02 coefficient copier is removed from these forks; coefficients are outside
this initial-state projection.

Each operation retains PostLoad, PostMerge and PostConversion exactly and adds
`observations.InitialDiscretization`. Capture.phases still has three Snapshot
entries; initial_discretization is a separate owner and callback count index3.
It copies the accepted passive callback after original Construction.cc619:
actual active Nodes/dx, counts, rcmax, reset NodeSource/NodeUserTemp, initial
CTFTimeStep/NumHistories and caller TimeStepZone. It never reruns a node formula.
Initial state is separate from whole-call return and retries at original908-936.

The selected pairing requires actual SourceSinkPresent=false/SolutionDimensions=1
owner context and an intact actual initial capture. AllR, unused, loading-error
and reversed routes can genuinely leave the callback unreached; they remain
unavailable/noPASS. No reverse flag or callback reachability is reconstructed.
A reached missing/invalid required field is an integrity failure. Actual reached
snapshots survive a later source fatal/exception, with that whole outcome retained
separately. OS failure without structured output gives no invented source ledger.

PostConversion remains required handoff context: actual dl/rk/rho/cp/lr/ResLayer,
LayersInConstruct/NumResLayers and active-prefix count. rho and cp are copied
capacitance factors, not a recomputed product. Original material membership stays
separate from merged local arrays; no normalized material IDs are invented.
Unused fixed tails and unassigned locals are never serialized.

Three fresh variable profiles (dx, initial_CTFTimeStep, caller_TimeStepZone) use
0.0 atol/rtol with exact class/shape/signed-zero rules. Nodes/counts/selectors/history
are exact integers. The inherited 18 preprocessing profiles stay unchanged as
separate context, and copied input/owner bits stay exact. No expected arrays,
branch outcomes, expected exits, or reference answers are supplied.

